1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,950
YA-NEC video course - lesson 0: the program in 5 minutes.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:16,950
Installation: download the zip for your system from Releases, extract it to a writable folder and start YA-NEC.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,017
YA-NEC course, lesson 0. When the program starts it is empty: no model open.

4
00:00:23,067 --> 00:00:29,981
Top bar: New, Open model, Save, Examples, then Calculate and Sweep.

5
00:00:30,031 --> 00:00:35,247
On the right: Ground, then at the very top Language and Colours.

6
00:00:35,297 --> 00:00:44,448
The fastest way to start: Examples. Here, a 20 m dipole at 10 m over average ground.

7
00:00:44,498 --> 00:00:51,581
The cards show the main results: impedance, SWR, gain, direction, F/B, beamwidth, frequency.

8
00:00:51,631 --> 00:00:55,153
The tabs below: Patterns...

9
00:00:55,203 --> 00:01:05,346
...Smith chart, Frequency (the sweep), back to the 3D structure.

10
00:01:05,396 --> 00:01:14,653
Open model reads other programs' files too.

11
00:01:14,703 --> 00:01:24,187
Formats: NEC2 (.nec), MMANA (.maa), AutoEZ/MultiNEC (.weq), EZNEC (.ez), K6STI YO (.yag) and AO (.ant), and YA-NEC's own .yanec.

12
00:01:24,237 --> 00:01:30,868
An AutoEZ file: the Delta Loop sample by AC6LA.

13
00:01:30,918 --> 00:01:36,868
AutoEZ variables and formulas are kept: the model opens ready to calculate.

14
00:01:36,918 --> 00:01:52,862
Now an MMANA file: IC8TEM's 4-element Box Kite for 144 MHz.

15
00:01:52,912 --> 00:01:58,462
MMANA notation, segmentation and sources are converted automatically.

16
00:01:58,512 --> 00:02:06,662
Save writes a NEC2 file, readable by every NEC program; calculators also save .yanec with everything inside.

17
00:02:06,712 --> 00:02:12,798
Settings: engine, ground, segmentation, patterns, losses.

18
00:02:12,848 --> 00:02:20,932
Bottom right: automatic update from GitHub. New versions arrive by themselves and start at the next launch.

19
00:02:20,982 --> 00:02:32,599
Colours: light, night, black, pastel... here Night, then back to Light.

20
00:02:32,649 --> 00:02:39,599
The full manual is inside the program, in the Manual tab (and as a PDF in the doc folder).

21
00:02:39,649 --> 00:02:44,600
Log records every operation: useful if something goes wrong.

22
00:02:44,650 --> 00:02:58,409
Self-test compares the engine with the values computed by nec2c on the same models.

23
00:02:58,459 --> 00:03:04,409
That is the program. From the next lesson we build antennas. YA-NEC is free: github.com/ic8tem/YA-NEC - 73 de IC8TEM
